---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Transport sketch"
  title="Wasserstein distance records how far mass moves"
  caption="Editorial point-mass example: P = δ₀ and Q = δₜ. Their supports are disjoint for every t > 0. The transport cost W₁ = t shrinks continuously as Q approaches P; symmetric JS with natural logarithms stays at log 2 until the supports coincide. Arrows represent movement of probability mass, not density heights or a measured training trajectory."
>
  <div class="wasserstein-panels">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 320 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="wgan-mass-title wgan-mass-desc">
      <title id="wgan-mass-title">Move a unit of probability mass</title>
      <desc id="wgan-mass-desc">One real point mass is at zero and one generated point mass is at t equals two. A horizontal arrow connects them. All the mass travels distance two, so the Wasserstein-1 distance is two.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="wgan-mass-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrow-head" />
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="160" y="22" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">All the mass has to travel</text>
      <text x="160" y="45" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Example: t = 2</text>
      <path d="M 34 210 H 288" class="axis" />
      <path d="M 70 204 V 216 M 230 204 V 216" class="axis" />
      <text x="70" y="238" text-anchor="middle">0</text>
      <text x="230" y="238" text-anchor="middle">t</text>
      <text x="285" y="237" text-anchor="end" class="muted">x</text>
      <path d="M 70 127 V 204" class="guide" />
      <path d="M 230 127 V 204" class="guide" />
      <circle cx="70" cy="210" r="5" class="real-point" />
      <circle cx="230" cy="210" r="5" class="generated-point" />
      <text x="70" y="110" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">P = δ₀</text>
      <text x="230" y="110" text-anchor="middle" class="accent panel-title">Q = δₜ</text>
      <path d="M 79 139 H 221" class="annotation" marker-end="url(#wgan-mass-arrow)" />
      <text x="150" y="161" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">move mass 1</text>
      <path d="M 70 265 V 275 H 230 V 265" class="annotation" />
      <text x="150" y="301" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">distance × mass = 2 × 1</text>
      <text x="150" y="324" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">No overlap is needed for a finite cost</text>
    </svg>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 320 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="wgan-cost-title wgan-cost-desc">
      <title id="wgan-cost-title">Wasserstein distance varies while Jensen-Shannon saturates</title>
      <desc id="wgan-cost-desc">For displacements t from zero to three, the Wasserstein-1 curve is a rising straight line from zero. The JS curve is constant at log two for positive t, with an open circle at zero and a separate filled point at the origin.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="wgan-cost-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrow-head" />
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="160" y="22" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">As Q approaches P</text>
      <text x="160" y="45" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Theoretical distances, t ≥ 0</text>
      <path d="M 48 70 V 250 H 286" class="axis" />
      <text x="50" y="63" class="muted">value</text>
      <text x="287" y="273" text-anchor="end" class="muted">t</text>
      {[0, 1, 2, 3].map((tick) => (
        <g>
          <path d={`M ${48 + tick * 74} 250 v 5`} class="axis" />
          <text x={48 + tick * 74} y="274" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">{tick}</text>
        </g>
      ))}
      <text x="36" y="254" text-anchor="end" class="muted">0</text>
      <text x="36" y="80" text-anchor="end" class="muted">3</text>
      <path d="M 48 250 L 270 76" class="wasserstein-line" />
      <text x="248" y="98" text-anchor="end" class="accent">W₁ = t</text>
      <path d="M 53 209.8 H 270" class="js-line" />
      <circle cx="48" cy="209.8" r="4" class="open-point" />
      <circle cx="48" cy="250" r="4" class="real-point" />
      <text x="273" y="197" text-anchor="end">JS = log 2</text>
      <path d="M 160 140 L 201 126" class="annotation" marker-end="url(#wgan-cost-arrow)" />
      <text x="88" y="135" class="accent">nonzero slope</text>
      <text x="160" y="305" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">JS drops to 0 only at t = 0</text>
      <text x="160" y="326" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">The plotted values use different units</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  .wasserstein-panels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 360px; height: auto; margin-inline: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 14px; }
  .panel-title { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; }
  .muted { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .accent { fill: var(--accent); }
  .axis { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; }
  .guide { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 3 4; }
  .real-point { fill: var(--ink); }
  .generated-point { fill: var(--accent); }
  .annotation, .arrow-head { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .wasserstein-line { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 2; }
  .js-line { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.6; stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .open-point { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) { .wasserstein-panels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; } }
</style>
